<section><h2>What cookies are</h2><p>Cookies are small text values stored by a browser so a website can remember a secure session, cart or preference between requests.</p></section><section><h2>Strictly necessary cookies</h2><p>WINNER uses necessary session, authentication and CSRF-security cookies. They enable login, verification, wishlist actions, cart contents, checkout protection and other requested functions. Disabling them in your browser may prevent these features from working.</p></section><section><h2>Cart and guest checkout</h2><p>The session keeps cart lines and checkout protections together. A guest order uses a private access token in its confirmation link rather than exposing order access through a cookie alone.</p></section><section><h2>Cookie preferences</h2><p>Your choice is stored in the <code>winner_cookie_consent</code> cookie. Rejecting optional cookies does not block necessary functionality. Use Cookie settings in the footer to change or revoke the preference.</p></section><section><h2>Optional cookies</h2><p>WINNER does not currently activate analytics or advertising cookies. If optional tools are introduced, they should remain inactive until an applicable preference permits them and this policy is updated.</p></section><section><h2>Retention and browser controls</h2><p>The preference cookie may remain for up to one year. Session-cookie duration follows server configuration. Browsers allow you to inspect, block or delete cookies, although doing so may sign you out or empty a session cart.</p></section><section><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about cookie use can be sent to winner.tennis999@gmail.com.</p></section>
